    "description": "Settings window: the sentence under Applies to, when the setting is stored in the project."
  },
  "settingsHelpSmoothThePictureWhenZoomed": "Off, a pixel magnified past 1:1 stays a square, which is what you zoom in to see. On, the picture is blended between pixels — softer, and easier on the eye when the zoom is for framing rather than for inspecting.",
  "@settingsHelpSmoothThePictureWhenZoomed": {
    "description": "Settings window: the sentence under the settingsSmoothThePictureWhenZoomed setting."
  },
  "settingsHelpShowTheToneMapButton": "Put the tone map button on the Viewer bar. Tone mapping folds a picture brighter than the screen can show back into what it can, so the detail up there can be seen while you work — it is a way of looking, and it never reaches an export. Off unless you ask for it.",
  "@settingsHelpShowTheToneMapButton": {
    "description": "Settings window: the sentence under the settingsShowTheToneMapButton setting. \"Up there\" means detail brighter than the display can show."
  },
  "settingsHelpSurroundTakesThemeColours": "Off, the area around the picture is a neutral grey — a grade cannot be judged against a tinted surround. On, it matches the rest of the shell.",
  "@settingsHelpSurroundTakesThemeColours": {
    "description": "Settings window: the sentence under the settingsSurroundTakesThemeColours setting."
  },
  "settingsHelpThisProcess": "What the system says Lumit is holding, all in — the number Activity Monitor and Task Manager show.",
